---
description: Scaffold a new plugin service following this plugin's architecture
---

Create a new service under `src/core/<area>/<Name>Service.ts`.

Match the existing services (Logger, SettingsService, VaultService, RequestService,
NoticeService, ModalService, CommandsService, EventBus):

- A focused class with constructor-injected dependencies — no reaching for the
  global `app`; take what it needs (`Plugin`, `Vault`, the `Logger`, …) as
  constructor args.
- Keep it in the `core` boundary zone: `core` may NOT import from `main` or `ui`
  (the fallow boundary gate enforces this at 0). Pure logic + Obsidian APIs only.
- Construct it in `main.ts`'s `onload` orchestration and expose it as a readonly
  field under a short name, so features and commands reach it through
  `plugin.<name>` (e.g. `plugin.commands`, `plugin.vault`), not `plugin.<name>Service`.
- No `console.*` (use the `Logger`); no raw `new Notice()` (use NoticeService);
  no raw HTML sinks.

Add a unit test `tests/unit/<name>Service.test.ts` that drives its public methods
against the obsidian mock, then run `{{run}} typecheck && {{run}} lint && {{run}} test`.
Keep `main.ts` orchestration-only — logic lives in the service, not the entry.

$ARGUMENTS
